  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support of Ukrainian Potato Sector with the implementation of European food and Phytosanitary requirements</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main goal of this project is to provide the Ukrainian Association of Potato Producers (UAPP) members and potential members with training and knowledge to comply with the new quality and quantity requirements in Ukraine. These requirements are related to changes in the Food Safety legislation and the consumer demand of potential new export markets. Members will receive training on various topics, including plant nutrition, fertilizers, crop protection chemicals, and identifying and addressing issues related to pests and diseases. The training aims to prepare the association for the technical requirements associated with the Deep and Comprehensive Free Trade Area (DCFTA).</narrative>
  </description>
